    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0200" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg182"/>

                <head>[Copy of protest given to the commander of the man-of-war <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aleut</hi>, 12th of August, 1891.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-12">August 12, 1891</date>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I, the undersigned, do hereby protest in behalf of the schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">James Hamilton Lewis</hi> and owners against the illegal
                    seizure of said vessel, her tackling and cargo, and hunting and fishing outfit,
                    by the Russian man-of-war <hi rendition="#italic">Aleut</hi>, the 2d day of
                    August, 1891, upon the high seas and neutral waters of the ocean. All seal skins
                    on board of said vessel had been killed upon said waters of the ocean with
                    shotguns, and the pup skins on board were taken from the inside of said seal
                    after they were taken on board of the vessel, and no seals were taken on board
                    of the vessel for forty hours previous to the said seizure. I therefore hold the
                    Russian man-of-war <hi rendition="#italic">Aleut</hi> and her Government
                    responsible for the detention and losses caused by the illegal seizure of said
                    vessel and outfit and cargo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander McLean</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Master of the Schooner “J. H. Lewis,” of San
                            Francisco, Cal., U. S. A.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
